WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.626
Wendy now had a daughter named Jane, who loved to hear her mother’s stories about Neverland.

2
00:00:06.627 --> 00:00:10.851
But most of all, Jane loved hearing about Peter.

3
00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:17.907
Wendy had bought her parents’ house, so Jane slept in the same nursery her mother had slept in as a girl.

4
00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:23.734
But there were only two beds now—one for Jane and one for her nanny.

5
00:00:23.735 --> 00:00:28.852
Once a week, on the nanny’s night off, Wendy would put Jane to bed.

6
00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:34.859
Then she would tell Jane wonderful stories about mermaids, fairies, and pirates.

7
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.382
"Tell me about when you were a little girl," Jane would begin sweetly.

8
00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:44.909
"That was a long time ago," her mother would answer.

9
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:50.023
"Tell me what it was like to fly," said the little girl one night.

10
00:00:50.024 --> 00:00:55.619
"You know, Jane, I can hardly remember. It was a long time ago."

11
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.087
"Why can’t you fly now, Mother?"

12
00:00:59.088 --> 00:01:04.446
"When people grow up, they forget how to fly," Wendy explained.

13
00:01:04.447 --> 00:01:09.503
She told Jane about the time Peter flew into the nursery looking for his shadow.

14
00:01:09.504 --> 00:01:15.729
"The foolish fellow tried to stick it on with soap and cried when it didn’t work," she said.

15
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.985
"But I sewed it back on for him."

16
00:01:18.986 --> 00:01:25.406
"Go on," said Jane impatiently, even though she knew all the stories by now.

17
00:01:25.407 --> 00:01:31.524
"And then he taught us how to fly and we flew to Neverland," said Wendy.

18
00:01:31.525 --> 00:01:36.349
"And what was the last thing he said to you?" asked Jane.

19
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:42.345
"He told me he would return, and some night I would hear him crowing by the window.

20
00:01:42.346 --> 00:01:47.770
But then he forgot all about me," Wendy said with a sad smile.

21
00:01:47.771 --> 00:01:54.026
"Funny, I sometimes hear that crow when I am sleeping," said Jane.

22
00:01:54.027 --> 00:01:57.594
And then one night something unusual happened.

23
00:01:57.595 --> 00:02:00.953
It was a spring night, and Jane was asleep.

24
00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:05.299
Wendy was in the darkened nursery, sewing in front of the fireplace.

25
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.239
Suddenly, she heard a crow.

26
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:14.376
The window blew open and Peter Pan flew in, landing lightly on the floor.

27
00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:17.476
"Hello, Wendy," he said.

28
00:02:17.477 --> 00:02:21.602
In the dim light, Peter didn’t notice that she had grown up.

29
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:25.361
As usual, he was thinking mostly about himself.

30
00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:29.921
For a moment, Wendy wished she could be as small as she used to be.

31
00:02:29.922 --> 00:02:33.274
"Hello, Peter," she replied.

32
00:02:33.275 --> 00:02:39.671
"Is that John in the bed there?" he asked, pointing to the small body under the sheet.

33
00:02:39.672 --> 00:02:44.010
"No, John is not here now," she said.

34
00:02:44.011 --> 00:02:49.799
Peter looked more closely. "Is it a new one? Boy or girl?"

35
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.949
"A girl," she replied, a bit fearfully.

36
00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.663
Peter looked at Wendy. "I’ve come to get you.

37
00:02:57.664 --> 00:03:01.613
Have you forgotten? It’s time for spring cleaning!"

38
00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:06.066
She knew it was useless to ask where he had been over the years.

39
00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:12.747
Instead she said, "I can’t come with you, Peter. I’ve forgotten how to fly."

40
00:03:12.748 --> 00:03:15.669
"I’ll teach you again," he said.

41
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:19.265
"Oh, Peter, don’t waste the fairy dust on me.

42
00:03:19.266 --> 00:03:23.420
I’ll turn on the light, and you’ll see for yourself."

43
00:03:23.421 --> 00:03:28.061
When she turned on the light, Peter gasped.

44
00:03:28.062 --> 00:03:32.367
"You promised not to grow up!" he shouted at her.

45
00:03:32.368 --> 00:03:35.340
"I couldn’t help it," she said.

46
00:03:35.341 --> 00:03:40.337
"I’m married now, and this is my little girl in the bed."

47
00:03:40.338 --> 00:03:43.626
Peter sat on the floor and began to weep.

48
00:03:43.627 --> 00:03:49.019
Wendy bent down to lift him up in her arms, but Peter backed away.

49
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.778
Seeing him so hurt, she left the room sadly.

50
00:03:52.779 --> 00:03:57.153
Peter’s sobs woke Jane. She sat up in bed.

51
00:03:57.154 --> 00:04:01.982
"Boy, why are you crying?" she asked.

52
00:04:01.983 --> 00:04:07.766
Peter rose and bowed politely. "Hello, I’m Peter Pan."

53
00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:15.007
"Yes, I know," said Jane. "I’m Jane, and I’ve been waiting for you."

54
00:04:15.008 --> 00:04:20.332
When Wendy returned, she found Peter sitting on Jane’s bed, crowing.

55
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:22.971
Jane was up in the air.

56
00:04:22.972 --> 00:04:27.547
"Jane wants to be my mother," Peter explained.

57
00:04:27.548 --> 00:04:32.937
"He does need a mother," Jane said, flying to his side.

58
00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:38.016
"Yes," Wendy said, "I know that very well."

59
00:04:38.017 --> 00:04:45.339
"He wants me to do his spring cleaning every year," Jane added, rising in the air with Peter.

60
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.381
"Good-bye, Wendy," said Peter, as they headed out into the night.

61
00:04:50.382 --> 00:05:02.336
Wendy rushed to the window crying, "No!" She stood there, watching them fly away together to Neverland, growing smaller and smaller in the sky.

62
00:05:02.337 --> 00:05:13.457
"If only I could go with them," she sighed.

